[blueprint]
format = 1
name = "Applet"
description = "Ocean Quick Menu applet: MainApplet.qml, applet.desktop and an icon"

[[file]]
path = "MainApplet.qml"
content = '''
import QtQuick
import OpenWave.QuickMenu as Applets

Applets.Applet {
    id: root
    property bool enabledState: false

    title: qsTr("@project_name@")
    icon: Qt.resolvedUrl("icon.svg")
    available: true
    active: enabledState
    statusText: active ? qsTr("On") : qsTr("Off")
    onTriggered: enabledState = !enabledState
}
'''

[[file]]
path = "applet.desktop"
content = '''
[Desktop Entry]
Type=X-OpenWave-Applet
Name=@project_name@
Comment=@project_name@ quick menu applet
Icon=icon.svg
X-OpenWave-Applet-Order=500
X-OpenWave-Applet-ApiVersion=1
'''

[[file]]
path = "icon.svg"
content = '''
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
  <circle cx="24" cy="24" r="15"/>
  <path d="M24 15v9l6 4"/>
</svg>
'''

[[file]]
path = "README.md"
content = '''
# @project_name@

An Ocean Quick Menu applet. The directory is the whole applet: `MainApplet.qml` is the only mandatory file,
`applet.desktop` and `icon.svg` are optional.

## Install

Copy this directory to your user applet location. The directory name is the applet id and must match
`[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63}`:

```sh
mkdir -p /Data/Users/$USER/.DataLocation/QuickMenu/Applets
cp -r . /Data/Users/$USER/.DataLocation/QuickMenu/Applets/@applet_name@
```

User applets are hidden until you enable them in Settings under Appearance, Quick Menu. System applets live in
`/System/QuickMenu/Applets/` and `/System/QuickMenu/Applets/Needed/` and are part of the system image.

## What an applet can use

`Applets.Applet` provides `title`, `icon`, `available`, `active`, `busy`, `statusText`, `interactive`, the
`triggered()` signal and the appearance colours. `Applets.System` exposes the narrow system operations the launcher
allows (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, flight mode, mobile data, lock and so on) and reports failure instead of pretending to
succeed. Applets run inside the launcher process, so keep them small and never block.

## applet.desktop

| key | meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `Name`, `Name[xx]` | display name and translations |
| `Comment` | description shown in Settings |
| `Icon` | svg or png path inside this directory |
| `X-OpenWave-Applet-Order` | position among applets, lower first |
| `X-OpenWave-Applet-ApiVersion` | must not exceed the version the launcher supports (1) |

Paths must be plain relative paths inside this directory without symbolic links. The `X-OpenWave-Applet-Settings`
key (a settings page under the applet in Settings) is honoured for system applets only.
'''
